a16z-waymo:greenhouse:7961706.descriptionHtml:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Waymo is an autonomous driving technology company with the mission to be the world&#39;s most trusted driver. Since its start as the Google Self-Driving Car Project in 2009, Waymo has focused on building the Waymo Driver—The World&#39;s Most Experienced Driver™—to improve access to mobility while saving thousands of lives now lost to traffic crashes. The Waymo Driver powers Waymo’s fully autonomous ride-hail service and can also be applied to a range of vehicle platforms and product use cases. The Waymo Driver has provided over ten million rider-only trips, enabled by its experience autonomously driving over 100 million miles on public roads and tens of billions in simulation across 15+ U.S. states.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Simulator team builds state-of-the-art simulations of realistic environments for the testing and training of the Waymo driver. We use machine learning to model the real world, including realistic agents (vehicles, pedestrians, cyclists, motorcyclists etc.), roads, traffic control systems, and weather. To increase the fidelity and steerability of the simulations, we employ large foundation models, trained on our massive datasets that allow us to quickly setup and rollout multiple scenarios to subject our driver to.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are planning to set up a team in London UK to work with the teams in MTV and Oxford to build these foundation models out and to integrate them into several evaluation and training products. We are looking for research engineers to work on these exciting problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this hybrid role, you will report to an Engineering Director.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be part of a world class research engineering team to grow the state-of-the-art of ultra realistic AV simulations using foundation models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with teams in Waymo Oxford to use large models to improve sim realism&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design experiments that push the frontiers of AV simulations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop metrics that measure the realism of simulated worlds&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Train and evaluate large models and integrate them into the simulator and its downstream applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help hire outstanding research engineers from diverse backgrounds&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be a part of a collaborative research engineering team that takes research ideas and productionizes them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We prefer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years experience in applied Deep Learning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years coding and design skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience solving complex production problems using state-of-the-art ML techniques&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience taking research to production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in Data Analysis or Data Science&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;The expected base salary range for this full-time position is listed below. Actual starting pay will be based on job-related factors, including exact work location, experience, relevant training and education, and skill level.&amp;nbsp; Waymo employees are also eligible to participate in Waymo’s discretionary annual bonus program, equity incentive plan, and generous Company benefits program, subject to eligibility requirements. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;£123,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;£129,000 GBP&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

a16z-xai:greenhouse:5127519007.descriptionHtml:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;ABOUT xAI&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;xAI’s mission is to create AI systems that can accurately understand the universe and aid humanity in its pursuit of knowledge. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Our team is small, highly motivated, and focused on engineering excellence. This organization is for individuals who appreciate challenging themselves and thrive on curiosity. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;We operate with a flat organizational structure. All employees are expected to be hands-on and to contribute directly to the company’s mission. Leadership is given to those who show initiative and consistently deliver excellence. Work ethic and strong prioritization skills are important. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;All employees are expected to have strong communication skills. They should be able to concisely and accurately share knowledge with their teammates.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a highly skilled Mechanical Commissioning Technician to support the buildout and startup of xAI’s high-performance data centers. In this critical hands-on role, you will perform commissioning, testing, and troubleshooting of mechanical systems that provide cooling, air handling, and fluid distribution for our next-generation AI supercomputing infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work closely with construction, engineering, and operations teams to ensure safe, reliable, and high-quality mechanical systems from initial installation through full system turnover. This is a full-time, onsite role with significant travel to xAI data center sites.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute mechanical commissioning activities for HVAC systems, chillers, cooling towers, CRAC/CRAH units, pumps, heat exchangers, piping systems, and associated controls in data center environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform functional testing, airflow and water flow verification, system balancing, and integrated system performance validation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot and resolve mechanical, controls, and hydronic issues during pre-commissioning, commissioning, and startup phases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute detailed commissioning test procedures, checklists, and documentation in accordance with project specifications and industry standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with EPC contractors, OEM vendors, and xAI engineers to coordinate system energization, startup sequences, and integrated system testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure strict adherence to safety protocols, LOTO procedures, and quality standards during all commissioning activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate as-built documentation, test records, and commissioning reports.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support training of operations and maintenance teams on commissioned mechanical systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in constructability reviews and provide field feedback to improve design and installation quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of hands-on mechanical commissioning or field technician experience in data centers, power plants, or large industrial facilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong working knowledge of data center cooling systems including chillers, cooling towers, pumps, CRAC/CRAH units, and precision air handling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with commissioning test equipment (manometers, anemometers, flow meters, temperature/pressure calibrators, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with relevant codes and standards (ASHRAE, SMACNA, NFPA, ASME, IMC).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to read and interpret mechanical drawings, P&amp;amp;IDs, and control schematics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong safety mindset with current OSHA 10/30 or equivalent training.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to work extended hours, nights, and weekends during critical commissioning windows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior commissioning experience on hyperscale data center projects or mission-critical facilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;NEBB, AABC, or equivalent certification in testing, adjusting, and balancing (TAB).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with BMS/BAS controls troubleshooting and integration (BACnet, Modbus, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of chilled water systems, refrigerant systems, and high-density liquid cooling technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with commissioning management software (e.g., CxPro, Procore, or similar).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical degree or trade school certification in Mechanical Engineering Technology, HVAC, or related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel extensively to xAI construction sites and remain onsite during peak commissioning phases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capability to work in industrial environments, climb ladders, lift moderate loads, and wear PPE for extended periods.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;xAI is an equal opportunity employer. For details on data processing, view our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.ai/legal/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

a16z-xai:greenhouse:5165458007.descriptionHtml:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;ABOUT xAI&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;xAI’s mission is to create AI systems that can accurately understand the universe and aid humanity in its pursuit of knowledge. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Our team is small, highly motivated, and focused on engineering excellence. This organization is for individuals who appreciate challenging themselves and thrive on curiosity. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;We operate with a flat organizational structure. All employees are expected to be hands-on and to contribute directly to the company’s mission. Leadership is given to those who show initiative and consistently deliver excellence. Work ethic and strong prioritization skills are important. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;All employees are expected to have strong communication skills. They should be able to concisely and accurately share knowledge with their teammates.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an exceptional &lt;strong&gt;Manager, Mechanical Engineering&lt;/strong&gt; to lead our Mechanical Engineering team within xAI’s Physical Infrastructure organization in Memphis. You will own the strategy, design, and delivery of mechanical systems for our high-density AI supercomputing facilities, with a strong emphasis on liquid cooling, HVAC, fluid systems, and structural mechanical infrastructure at massive scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this leadership role, you will manage a team of mechanical engineers while directly contributing to technical decisions. You will collaborate closely with thermal, electrical, power, construction, commissioning, and operations teams to deliver reliable, efficient, and scalable infrastructure that supports xAI’s rapidly growing compute demands. This is a full-time, onsite role based in the Memphis region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and mentor a team of Mechanical Engineers, providing technical guidance, performance feedback, and professional development while driving accountability for project deliverables.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end mechanical design strategy for AI data center infrastructure, including liquid cooling loops, cold plates, manifolds, heat exchangers, server enclosures, structural supports, facility HVAC systems, and related MEP integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and evolve mechanical standards, design guidelines, and best practices to ensure performance, reliability, manufacturability, cost-effectiveness, and scalability across current and future facilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform and oversee complex engineering analyses (thermal, fluid dynamics, structural, CFD, FEA) to optimize systems and meet extreme density, efficiency, and uptime targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and review specifications, 3D models, drawings, BOMs, test plans, and commissioning procedures; support prototyping, qualification, and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-functional collaboration on new facility designs, cluster expansions, and retrofits, balancing performance, schedule, budget, and operational requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interface with vendors, contractors, and suppliers for equipment selection, fabrication, installation, and successful commissioning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct failure mode analysis (FMEA), root cause investigations, and reliability modeling; drive corrective actions and lessons learned into future designs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage project priorities, resources, and risks within the mechanical engineering scope while supporting broader infrastructure program goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay current with industry advancements in data center cooling, sustainable design, and mechanical technologies to maintain xAI’s competitive edge.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Mechanical Engineering or a related engineering discipline (Master’s or PE license preferred).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in mechanical system design, with at least 3 years in a leadership or people-management role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong background in data center or industrial facility mechanical systems (liquid cooling, HVAC, fluid handling).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience leading mechanical engineering teams in hyperscale data centers, critical facilities, or high-density compute environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in liquid cooling technologies, chilled water systems, heat exchangers, airflow management, and integration with power and building systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with engineering tools such as CFD (e.g., ANSYS, FloTHERM), FEA, AutoCAD, Revit, and BIM workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of relevant codes and standards (ASHRAE, NFPA, IBC, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with construction project management, contractor oversight, commissioning, and vendor management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of delivering complex mechanical infrastructure projects on time and within budget while maintaining high reliability and efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to thrive in a fast-paced, ambiguous environment with ownership of outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and collaboration skills, with the ability to influence cross-functional stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Physical ability to perform hands-on work in various environments, including heat, cold, rain, and tight quarters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work extended hours and weekends as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel occasionally as required by project needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Valid driver&#39;s license.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lift up to 25 lbs. unassisted.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;xAI is an equal opportunity employer. For details on data processing, view our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.ai/legal/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

a16z-zipline:greenhouse:7666183003.descriptionHtml:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About Zipline&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zipline is the world’s largest and most experienced drone delivery service. We are on a mission to serve all humans equally by ensuring access to food, medicine and essential goods anytime, anywhere. We design, build, and operate the world’s largest autonomous logistics system, delivering critical supplies quickly and reliably. Today, Zipline operates on four continents, makes a delivery somewhere in the world every 30 seconds, and has completed millions of deliveries to date, including blood, vaccines, medical supplies, food, and retail products.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our customers include the world’s largest and most prominent healthcare systems, governments, retailers, restaurants and global businesses who rely on us to save lives, reduce emissions, increase economic opportunity, and provide delivery from point A to point B as fast as possible. The drone is only 15% of what we’ve built to enable seamless, reliable, global operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our system strengthens supply chains, reduces congestion, and gives people time back. With more than 140 million commercial autonomous miles safely flown, Zipline is redefining access to healthcare, consumer products, and food across the globe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We operate at a global scale and are looking for practical problem solvers who thrive on real-world challenges and rapid growth. Our team is motivated by building systems that have a direct, meaningful impact on people’s lives and by scaling the future of logistics. We are seeking people who sculpt from first principles, enjoy facing adversity, and can do the impossible at record breaking speeds.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You and The Role&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Head of Corporate Finance is a critical leadership role on Zipline’s Strategic Finance team and sits at the center of how the company plans, measures, and communicates financial performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This leader will own Zipline’s company-wide financial planning, forecasting, and reporting infrastructure, building the financial backbone that powers decision-making across the business. You will lead the company’s planning cadence, maintain the consolidated global business model, and ensure leadership has a clear, consistent understanding of company performance and long-term strategy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will partner closely with Strategic Finance, Accounting, G&amp;amp;A teams, and Executive Leadership to ensure Zipline’s financial processes and reporting are rigorous, scalable, and aligned with published standards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Just as importantly, you will help elevate the entire Strategic Finance organization, building the systems, tools, and processes that allow the company to move quickly while maintaining financial discipline as Zipline scales globally and prepares for the public markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role will be an in-person role based at our HQ in South San Francisco.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own Zipline’s Global Financial Planning &amp;amp; Forecasting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain Zipline’s consolidated global financial model, integrating actuals and forecasts across all departments and business lines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the company’s annual planning and quarterly forecast processes across Strategic Finance and the broader organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define planning workstreams, ownership, timelines, and outputs to ensure a tight, efficient process with clear leadership decision points.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with business leaders to evaluate investment tradeoffs and align financial plans with Zipline’s strategic priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead the Company’s Financial Operating Cadence&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead monthly forecast-to-actual reviews with finance leadership and executives, ensuring clear visibility into performance drivers and emerging risks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish Zipline’s management reporting framework and financial metrics that serve as the company’s source of truth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the creation of executive reporting materials and board decks that communicate company performance and strategic progress.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive Long-Range Planning and Strategic Financial Modeling&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage Zipline’s long-range financial plan, including maintenance of the company’s five-year plan which is used for investor communication, fundraising, and long-term capital planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build scenario models that evaluate strategic investments, capital requirements, and growth pathways.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strengthen Financial Infrastructure and Reporting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the systems, tools, and processes that power Strategic Finance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously elevate Zipline’s financial systems, data infrastructure, and planning tools to improve speed, accuracy, and insight generation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Accounting to improve financial reporting structures, account coding, and reporting systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure financial reporting accurately reflects business performance while aligning with external reporting standards and IPO readiness requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead G&amp;amp;A Business Partnership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary financial partner to G&amp;amp;A functions including People, Legal, Facilities, and Finance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own company-wide headcount forecasting and workforce planning in partnership with the People Team, Strategic Finance and Executive Leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build operating cost plans that support company goals while maintaining financial discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support Investor Communication and IPO Readiness&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support investor updates and reporting by ensuring consistent, high-quality financial materials and narratives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help prepare Zipline for the operational and reporting requirements of public markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Accounting, Legal, and leadership to build the financial discipline and reporting infrastructure required for IPO readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You&#39;ll Bring&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in strategic finance, corporate finance, investment banking, consulting, or financial strategy within high-growth organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience owning company-wide planning, forecasting, and financial modeling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and improving financial reporting systems and planning infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong track record partnering with senior executives to drive company-level decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in financial modeling, forecasting, and scenario analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication skills, with the ability to translate complex financial data into clear insights for executives, boards, and investors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong leadership instincts with the ability to build systems, develop teams, and drive operational rigor across the organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for mission-driven work and for building the financial infrastructure that enables breakthrough technology to scale globally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience preparing companies for IPO or operating in public-company environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience scaling financial planning systems or ERP/FP&amp;amp;A tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in logistics, marketplaces, robotics, or operations &amp;amp; hardware-heavy businesses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience working with Boards or investors in high-growth companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What Else You Need to Know&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The starting cash range for this role is $200,000-$240,000, plus equity. Please note that this is a target, starting cash range for a candidate who meets the minimum qualifications for this role. The final cash pay for this role will depend on a variety of factors, including a specific candidate&#39;s experience, qualifications, skills, working location, and projected impact. The total compensation package for this role may also include: discretionary annual or performance bonuses; sales incentives; benefits such as medical, dental and vision insurance; paid time off; and more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zipline is an equal opportunity employer and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, ancestry, national origin, religion or religious creed, mental or physical disability, medical condition, genetic information, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, and related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, marital status, military or veteran status, citizenship, or other characteristics protected by state, federal or local law or our other policies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We value diversity at Zipline and welcome applications from those who are traditionally underrepresented in tech. If you like the sound of this position but are not sure if you are the perfect fit, please apply!&lt;/p&gt;

abstractvc-garner-health:greenhouse:6005.descriptionHtml:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Garner’s mission is to transform the healthcare economy, delivering high-quality and affordable care for all.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are fundamentally reimagining how healthcare works in the U.S. by partnering with employers to redesign healthcare benefits using clear incentives and powerful, data-driven insights. Our approach guides employees to higher-quality, lower-cost care, creating a system that works better for everyone. Patients achieve better health outcomes, employers spend healthcare dollars more effectively, and physicians are rewarded for delivering exceptional care rather than performing more procedures.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Garner is one of the fastest-growing healthcare technology companies in the country. Our products are trusted by the most sophisticated employers and providers in the industry, and we are building a team of talented, mission-driven individuals who are motivated to make a meaningful impact on healthcare at scale.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an exceptional &lt;strong&gt;Growth Marketing Strategy &amp;amp; Marketing Ops Manager &lt;/strong&gt;to join our&lt;strong&gt; Growth Marketing &lt;/strong&gt;team (under the Product org). This role will report to the VP of Growth Marketing.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will define and shape how we will drive Garner adoption at our largest clients. You’ll own the engagement strategy at our clients and launch marketing campaigns (e.g., email, SMS, direct mail, creating custom marketing assets) to drive member sign-ups and engagement with Garner. You will serve as the strategic marketing partner to our Client Management teams. As Garner scales fast, you will also be responsible for building scalable, automated, and efficient processes and tools (including building AI tools). This is a highly strategic and collaborative role at the heart of our growth engine - helping us engage more members&amp;nbsp;and ultimately improve health outcomes at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Where you will work:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will be based in our New York City office (in the Financial District). You must be willing to work in the office 3 days per week on Tuesday, Wednesday and Thursday.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead marketing strategy &amp;amp; execution at clients:&lt;/strong&gt; You will own the strategy and execution of custom multi-channel communication strategies at key clients in your book of business, aligned to their unique employee demographics, communication channels, and business objectives.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Develop and execute custom client marketing campaigns: &lt;/strong&gt;You will launch multi-channel campaigns (e.g., email, SMS, direct mail, employer-sent communications on Garner) and leverage marketing automation tools (Iterable) to build &amp;amp; optimize campaigns. You’ll develop new assets for our marketing asset library - including custom marketing collateral for our largest clients - working with our designers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Serve as an expert consultant to Sales, Client Management, and Clients:&lt;/strong&gt; You will serve as a trusted strategic advisor and subject matter expert, making sure stakeholders understand Garner’s approach to engagement. You’ll also pilot marketing campaigns at key clients and work with the broader Growth Marketing team to scale proven engagement tactics across the rest of our book of business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analyze data to measure &amp;amp; optimize campaign performance:&lt;/strong&gt; You will own a data-driven approach to performance measurement and optimization by providing regular client-specific reporting on marketing performance to clients and internal stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build Scalable Processes &amp;amp; AI tools:&lt;/strong&gt; You will automate workflows and build AI tools for engagement marketing - making us more efficient in how we work with stakeholders and how we track, strategize, and execute on member engagement.&amp;nbsp; &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The idea candidate has:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5+ &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;years &lt;/strong&gt;of experience in member engagement, lifecycle marketing / user acquisition, marketing ops, growth marketing, client services, and/or growth marketing. Experience from a management consulting firm, high-growth start-up, marketing agency, or digital health tech company is preferred&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Understanding of cross-channel&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;marketing platforms&lt;/strong&gt;, preferably &lt;strong&gt;Iterable, &lt;/strong&gt;and tactical execution of email, segment, and campaign builds&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Basic design experience&lt;/strong&gt; for marketing collateral (e.g., Google Slides, Figma)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive-level communication and presentation skills&lt;/strong&gt;, with the ability to articulate complex marketing concepts to internal and external stakeholders&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Results-oriented strategic thinker &amp;amp; problem solver &lt;/strong&gt;who can break down ambiguous, complex problems, proactively identify opportunities, and translates vision into action - all while managing multiple complex client initiatives simultaneously&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bias for innovative &amp;amp; experimentation&lt;/strong&gt;, constantly seeking to test new growth tactics and channels and partner with cross-functional stakeholders to bring new ideas to life&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborative leader who builds strong relationships &lt;/strong&gt;across internal teams (Sales, Client Management, Product, Data) and with senior client stakeholders&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A self-starter&lt;/strong&gt; with the ability to thrive in a fast-paced, dynamic start-up environment&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A desire to be a part of a &lt;strong&gt;high-performing, mission-driven team&lt;/strong&gt; that operates with intense urgency, a strong sense of individual accountability, and a commitment to authentic feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a unique opportunity to join a fast-growing company in a transformative role, helping shape the future of healthcare.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation Transparency:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The target salary range for this position is $145,000 - $170,000. Individual compensation for this role will depend on various factors, including qualifications, skills, and applicable laws. In addition to base compensation, this role is eligible to participate in our equity incentive and competitive benefits plans, including but not limited to: flexible PTO, Medical/Dental/Vision plan options, 401(k) with company match, flexible spending accounts, Teladoc Health and more.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fraud and Security Notice:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please be aware of recent job scam attempts. Our recruiters use &lt;a href=&quot;http://getgarner.com/&quot;&gt;getgarner.com&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;garnerhealth.com&quot;&gt;garnerhealth.com&lt;/a&gt; email domains exclusively. If you have been contacted by someone claiming to be a Garner recruiter or a hiring manager from a different domain about a potential job, please report it to law enforcement &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.ic3.gov/Home/ComplaintChoice&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt; and to &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:candidateprotection@getgarner.com&quot;&gt;candidateprotection@garnerhealth.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Employment Opportunity:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
Garner Health is proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity employer and values diversity in the workplace. We do not discriminate based upon race, religion, color, national origin, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, reproductive health decisions, or related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, status as a protected veteran, status as an individual with a disability, genetic information, political views or activity, or other applicable legally protected characteristics.
&lt;p&gt;Garner Health is committed to providing accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities in our recruiting process. If you need assistance or an accommodation due to a disability, you may contact us at &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:talent@getgarner.com&quot;&gt;talent@garnerhealth.com&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

